From ee89be1f9bf6bf258572e5a818e87721e5e6ebd3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "sh.chao" <sh.chao@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 20 Jul 2026 12:57:27 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] r25-2-0093: compile owned opaque line commands in shadow mode

Extend the r25 + 0051 + 0075-0076 + r25-2-0092 generation-2 baseline with the first self-owned native primitive. During the existing parser append, copy exact two-point opaque stroke geometry and intern bitwise-exact matrix, color, dash, cap, join, width, miter, and stroke-adjust state.

Keep one opcode per holder object in exact painter order. Leave the first 4096 commands canonical and begin shadow compilation only for a large-holder suffix, without a second scan, so normal pages do no native eligibility or payload work. Reject clips, marked content, fills, transparency, transfer functions, overprint, patterns, non-finite data, unsupported geometry, and exhausted tables to canonical path opcodes.

Use fixed-size line chunks and hard command/state/matrix/dash ceilings; retain no CPDF_PageObject pointer. This revision is shadow-only: legacy PathDL remains disabled and canonical PDFium remains the sole pixel owner. Add large-holder telemetry and ownership, state-interning, canonical-fallback tests so 0094 can validate coverage and memory before enabling a visible subset.
